"I built a Helpdesk Ticket Management System for a two-person IT support team. The main problem is that the ticket queue continuously grows and the team needs to know which ticket should be handled next.

I implemented a Flask backend with SQLite for persistence and a JavaScript-based frontend.

The core business logic is the priority queue. Tickets are automatically ordered using overdue status first, then priority — URGENT, HIGH, NORMAL and LOW — followed by the earliest deadline and creation time as tie-breakers.

I also implemented the additional escalation requirement. When an active ticket breaches its response deadline, the system automatically increases its priority by one level. For example, NORMAL becomes HIGH and HIGH becomes URGENT. An URGENT ticket cannot be escalated further, and only one level is changed per escalation run.

The application provides ticket creation, search, filtering, assignment, status management, deletion and dashboard statistics.

I separated the application into different modules: app.py handles APIs, database.py handles persistence, queue.py handles queue ordering, escalation.py handles escalation, and the frontend files handle the user interface.

